            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "shouldn't need a bitmask. maybe i got confused at some point while reviewing the other pr (and it's good we're doing this separately here).\r\n\r\nthink about what is mutually-exclusive and what isn't. \r\n\r\n- any \"kinds\" which are mutually-exclusive should be in `WinKind`.\r\n- non-exclusive stuff can stay as `w_foo` booleans.\r\n\r\n```\r\nw_floating  // boolean\r\nw_kind      // normal/preview/info  <= these are mutually-exclusive\r\n```\r\n\r\nthis is only a suggestion; please think about the best approach\r\n\r\nif the above looks good, then maybe we dont need a `win_is_float` function, bc the `w_is_float` boolean suffices.",
            "created_at": "2026-07-19T12:13:41Z",
